SwiftPutty local patch 0023
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; suitable for upstream

GSSAPI authentication: free the MIC once it is in the packet.

ssh2_userauth_gss_packet() gets a MIC from the GSSAPI library with
get_mic(), copies it into the outgoing packet, and never released it
with free_mic(), so each gssapi-with-mic or gssapi-keyex login leaked
the library's buffer. Found by `leaks --atExit` on
Core/tests/spb_ssh_test.c logging in to a Kerberos test realm.

--- a/ssh/userauth2-client.c
+++ b/ssh/userauth2-client.c
@@ -2575,6 +2575,7 @@
         put_stringz(p, authtype);
     }
     put_string(p, mic.value, mic.length);
+    s->shgss->lib->free_mic(s->shgss->lib, &mic);
 
     return p;
 }
